<title>GERMANY: German air controllers count 24 near misses in '96.</title>
<headline>German air controllers count 24 near misses in '96.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German air traffic controllers said on Tuesday 24 near-misses in German airspace were reported in 1996 compared to 23 the year before.</p>
<p>The Deutsche Flugsicherung (DFS) national air traffic control company said that with German air traffic having risen by nearly four percent in 1996, the figures confirmed that the country's airspace was still safe.</p>
<p>DFS said a large part of the incidents involved private or military pilots.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
